# Nested git worktrees hold a full second copy of this repo. They are gitignored
# (see .gitignore), but Prettier does not consult .gitignore — so an ad-hoc
# `prettier --write .` from the repo root would rewrite files inside another
# session's worktree. Keep these patterns in sync with .gitignore:38-41.
.claude/worktrees/
worktrees/
.worktrees/
.codex-worktrees/
*-worktrees/

# Generated by `bun run audit:cross-domain`, whose `--check` mode (the CI gate
# in pr-web.yaml) compares the file byte for byte against freshly serialized
# output. Prettier collapses the single-element arrays that
# `JSON.stringify(..., null, 2)` expands, so formatting this file makes the
# gate fail on a diff with no content change. The generator is its formatter.
clients/web/.cross-domain-allowlist.json
